Hello All --

I received some good advice from Dr. Flemming and just wanted to follow up with a couple of other questions.

Using "weights=TRUE" in the adke function made a seemingly beneficial improvement with regard to the fit of the kernel.  Would you suggest using this as a default setting in most cases?

Also, I am uncertain as to how to obtain the model fit results for all the anisotrophic and isotrophic models?  I looked in the FAQ for AIC info, but could not find any (may be user error)?  Sorry for the confusion.  Any guidance here would be great.

Thanks for any input.

